    "font size" : 15.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "4.4 Configuring user authentication"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 84,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 136.0, 170.0, 534.0, 180.667 ],
    "font" : "Helvetica",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "There are two methods of user authentication to control access to the GUI and to the CLI:"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 85,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 149.333, 126.382, 533.667, 165.333 ],
    "font" : "Helvetica",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Local authentication is performed within the Storwize V7000 system. Local GUI authentication is done with user name and password. Local CLI authentication is done either with an SSH public key or a user name and password."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 86,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 150.333, 61.667, 546.333, 124.0 ],
    "font" : "Helvetica",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Remote authentication allows users to authenticate to the system using credentials stored on an external authentication service. This feature allows you to use user credentials and user groups defined on the remote service to simplify user management and access, enforce password policies more efficiently, and separate user management from storage management."
  } ]
}